## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a stateful, TTL-based enrichment with side-input updates, late-data handling, and idempotent sinks in KCNA. Reflects real-world needs for per-user enrichment at scale.

## Key Concepts
- TTL-based in-memory caches for streaming enrichment
- Side-input stream for cache population
- Exactly-once vs at-least-once semantics in sinks
- Re-enrichment triggers and idempotent downstream writes
- Offset management across multi-topic joins

## Code Example
```javascript
// Skeleton enrichment logic
class Enricher {
  constructor(ttlMs) {
    this.cache = new TTLCache(ttlMs); // maps userId -> segment
  }
  enrichMessage(clickEvent) {
    const seg = this.cache.get(clickEvent.userId);
    if (seg) return { ...clickEvent, segment: seg };
    // emit with unknown and schedule re-enrichment on cache update
    return { ...clickEvent, segment: 'unknown' };
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test eviction and re-enrichment without data loss?
- How would you scale the TTL cache across multiple workers?
- How would you detect and recover from cache corruption or delays in side-inputs?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests encryption design, tenancy isolation, rotation semantics, cross-region distribution, and auditability in KCNA.

## Key Concepts
- Envelope encryption with per-tenant KEK and DEK
- KMS integration, key-versioning, and cross-region propagation
- Zero-downtime rotation and background re-wrapping
- Audit trails and RBAC for keys

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: envelope encrypt a payload
function encryptPayload(plaintext, tenantId, kmsClient) {
  const DEK = kmsClient.getDataKey(tenantId);
  const wrappedDEK = kmsClient.wrapKey(DEK, tenantId);
  const ciphertext = cryptoAesGCM(nonce, DEK, plaintext);
  return { ciphertext, wrappedDEK, keyVersion: kmsClient.currentVersion(tenantId) };
}

function decryptPayload(payloadPkg, tenantId, kmsClient) {
  const DEK = kmsClient.unwrapKey(payloadPkg.wrappedDEK, tenantId);
  return cryptoAesGCMDecrypt(payloadPkg.ciphertext, DEK);
}
```

